# Menu icons

Two menu styles exist. Pick the one that matches the surface; do not mix icon styles in one menu.

## VS Code–style context menus (preferred for tree / right-click)

See skill `vscode-context-menu`.

- **Default: text only** — no leading icons. Submenu chevron on the right is OK.
- Reference: `TreeContextMenu` + `.tree-context-menu.is-plaintext`.
- **Icons only if the user explicitly asks** for them on that menu: then use **monochrome** VS Code–style glyphs (`currentColor` stroke/outline, size 16) — not Flat Color (`Fc*`).
- Panel/items stay neutral (`dropdown-menus.mdc`); no accent hover fill.

## Create menus & button dropdowns (Flat Color)

Product **create menus** and **button dropdown menus** that still use leading icons use **Flat Color** from `react-icons/fc`.

- Shared wrappers: `src/components/menuIcons.tsx`, document kinds in `src/components/treeIcons.tsx`.
- Size **16** in menus; tree/tab file icons may use 14–20.
- Do **not** put monochrome stroke icons next to Flat Color icons in the same menu.
- Do **not** tint Flat Color icons with `--accent`.
- Destructive rows: `.is-danger` on the item; icon may stay the Flat Color trash glyph.
- Toolbar chrome that is **not** a menu may keep monochrome SVG when `currentColor` / animation is required.

## Migrating an old context menu

When restyling a context menu to the VS Code look: drop Flat Color leading icons, apply plaintext gutter padding, keep English labels and separators. Add monochrome icons only on explicit request.
